  "label": "Repetition as Simple Identity",
  "description": "The use of repetition in self-introduction ('bob... bob') to imply simplicity or lack of depth, which is a common trope in ableist humor and media portrayals. This reinforces the idea that individuals with developmental disabilities are incapable of complex or unique self-expression.",
